WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.910
What makes worldbuilding so important in Anime
and Manga?

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.860
What sets these two apart as genres from other
forms of storytelling is their unique use

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.990
of visual elements.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.690
Compared to a novel, that is purely text-based
and relies completely on describing every

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:29.020
bit of context that the author wants to convey
using words, a Manga embeds its dialog and

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:35.300
plot into a visual framework for the reader
to see and feel, rather than read and interpret.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.860
In essence it allows capturing the most significant
moments of a story, by combining two mediums

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.460
at the same time: Film and text.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.030
Every panel in the story is like a frozen
frame, carefully chosen to catch THE instant

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.060
carrying the best meaning and emotion for
the reader.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:57.140
In the hands of the right person, this hybrid
form can allow for a unique way of storytelling,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.210
combining the advantages of visual and textual
elements.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:05.390
While it gives us the effortless feeling of
watching a scene unfold on screen, it still

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.049
manages to retain the readers need for interpretation
and in extension also participation in the

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:12.049
story.

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:17.240
By only showing us a fraction of what is happening,
a moment captured in time, and nothing but

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.600
plain text for dialogs and description, Manga
leaves a lot more to the reader than a movie

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.970
would, while still showing a much clearer
picture of the world than any book could do.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:33.020
Anime then of course takes this a step further
and brings that story into the medium of film

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.020
completely.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.799
Being able to witness a story unfold by seeing
the characters actions and emotions with your

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:42.450
own eyes can without any doubt be a great
experience.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.700
However, as you probably are aware, emotions
and thoughts can be depicted in a non-visual

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:52.429
way just as well and in some cases maybe in
even more detail.

00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:57.280
The true power then of the visual nature of
Anime and Manga lies somewhere else.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.630
What really affects its audience the most
and what makes this genre so intriguing for

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:06.159
people to follow is the vast and rich story
world it creates.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:09.890
In other words, worldbuilding.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:16.140
I think everyone has made the experience of
becoming obsessed with the world of a story

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.150
they love.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.840
This obsession becomes strikingly clear when
looking at franchises like Game of Thrones,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.180
Harry Potter or the Lord of the Rings, where
worldbuilding has been taken to an entirely

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.460
new level.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.739
What makes these vast worlds, with deep-reaching
lore, countless regions and even unique languages

00:02:33.739 --> 00:02:39.400
so fascinating to us, is our desire loose
ourselves in the stories we love.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.730
We are looking for a way to keep the story
going and explore even more of its facets

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.409
and adventures.

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:50.340
However, simply cramming as much detail and
additional information into your storytelling

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.439
won´t make people fall in love with it.

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:56.590
A lesson that many authors and writers have
had to learn before.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.020
Great worldbuilding then is a lot more than
simply overloading the audience with heaps

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.340
of information and impressive visuals.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.299
In fact, introducing more and more elements
of a world, that don't directly influence

00:03:08.299 --> 00:03:13.239
the story at hand can lead to a rapid drop
in tension in your story line and ultimately

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:16.000
result in the audience losing interest.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.770
So, what makes a good story world?

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:25.420
What sets this world you enjoy losing yourself
in apart from others?

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.390
In a good story, the world is a representation
of the inner and more personal struggles of

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.860
the protagonist.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.650
It is a physical representation of the most
essential elements of storytelling.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.810
Conflict, emotion, symbolism and development.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:45.300
All these things, that drive the plot and
get you involved into the characters and their

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:49.430
actions, have to be connected to the world
this story takes place in in some way or form.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:54.610
So, it is important that each new element
of the physical story world has a connection

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:58.940
to the events at hand and enrich the context
under which they take place.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:04.080
Once the arena resonates with the plot, the
audience now can start to enrich and expand

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.480
this world in their own mind, without needing
any specific instructions.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.859
Now we actually want to know more about this
universe, that has brought forth and shaped

00:04:12.859 --> 00:04:14.290
our hero.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:18.640
This way, we assure that the plot and the
characters involved, feel like an organic

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.590
part of the world they are in.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:25.170
Their struggles and the world´s struggles
now go hand in hand.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.540
So how is such a story world created?

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.630
How does it influence your perception of the
story?

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:36.420
And even more specifically why does it make
Manga and Anime so enjoyable to watch?

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.710
We will now explore these questions using
the example of One Piece.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.140
But once you finish this video you will be
able to apply these principals to any other

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.970
great story you encounter.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:52.840
And no worries, plot wise this case study
will be 100% spoiler free.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:57.620
If you are unfamiliar with the story of One
Piece, it follows the adventures of a young

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:04.000
pirate, Monkey D. Luffy and his crew to explore
the world and become the King of the pirates.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.920
This may sound weird at first, but the overarching
premise of the story is already deeply connected

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.900
to the story world it occurs in.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.540
Because the world of One Piece IS actually
a world of pirates.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:21.980
The arena for our story is an entire planet,
that is mostly covered by ocean.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:26.660
With the exception of a single slim continent,
that spans around the globe like a wall and

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:31.510
is inaccessible to all but a small ruling
class, all inhabitable land exists in the

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.900
form of islands spread across the world.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:38.720
This ruling class dominates the entire population
of the world.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:43.840
The only exception to this are pirates, who
roam the oceans freely and openly oppose the

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.550
control and rules set by this world government.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:52.380
The evil rulers live on top of this single
continuous landmass, that separates the world,

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.250
looking down on the rest of people.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:59.800
A dangerous and wild ocean called the Grand
Line splits the world in the other direction,

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:02.610
forming four isolated regions.

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:06.720
This world is constructed in a way that keeps
people from moving around and interacting

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.200
with others.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:13.020
As you can see, the story world already is
a physical representation of the political

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:17.970
structures as well as of the resulting injustice
and suppression happening in this world.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:22.520
The only ones that DO move around freely are
those that oppose the regime.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:27.590
And since the world is completely made up
of water and islands, these people are pirates,

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:31.660
thus the premise of the plot being a pirate
story.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.680
This is the system and environment our hero
lives in.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.870
Now take a moment and think about this world.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.520
Just by looking at its physical structure
and geography, can you tell what the overarching

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.310
struggle in the story will be?

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:48.650
It´s actually really clear right?

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.710
Even if you know nothing about the story of
One Piece, you guessed that this will be a

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:56.310
story about gaining freedom and changing the
world.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.500
To fulfill this goal, our protagonist is sent
on a journey through this arena.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:05.880
And while this world has many different facets,
regions and cultures, the overarching threat

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.990
posed by the world government does not change,
no matter where you go.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:15.500
So, while it feels like we are changing places
a lot, the overarching arena stays the same.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:20.440
However, this arena will have to change over
time, as the hero changes in it.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:25.120
So, while Luffy is on a journey to become
the pirate king, the freest person in the

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:31.180
world, this goal actually also implies destroying
the current system of oppression and changing

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.800
the world itself.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.850
The hero´s struggle is the world´s struggle.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.870
By becoming free himself, he frees the world.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:42.180
This is what makes the story feel so organic.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:46.850
The characters we meet are a real part of
this universe and not just a group of people

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.490
dropped onto a nice-looking stage.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:54.260
So now that we looked at the overall structure
of a story world, let´s get a little bit

00:07:54.260 --> 00:08:00.860
more into the specific details of worldbuilding.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:06.010
One of the most prominent elements of any
story world is the natural setting that serves

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:08.980
as a framework for the plot to take place.

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:13.730
Typical examples from nature are the mountains,
the forest or the desert, while there are

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:17.970
also man-made spaces like cities or villages.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:22.840
Each of these settings has a unique set of
characteristics and implications for the story,

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.740
that go far beyond simple geography.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:30.570
To explain this a little more in depth, let´s
look at the two most prominent natural settings

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:35.340
in the story of One Piece: The Ocean and the
island.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:39.390
The ocean makes up large parts of the planet
One Piece takes place on.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:45.360
As a stage for our plot, it can once again
be divided into two distinct zones: The surface

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.089
and the depths.

00:08:47.089 --> 00:08:50.959
The surface is the ultimate 2-dimensional
landscape.

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:55.750
Like a huge chessboard, it is the playing
field for the characters, with islands sprinkled

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:57.139
across the map.

00:08:57.139 --> 00:09:01.089
It is here that the journey between the different
destination takes place and where weather

00:09:01.089 --> 00:09:06.250
phenomena and other ships are the only other
encounters for the crew.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:11.600
The surface is a representation of the freedom
that the hero is yearning and it´s infinite

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:16.560
horizon opens up to an infinite number of
possible destinations.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:21.899
On the other hand, the depths of the ocean
are the ultimate 3-dimensional space.

00:09:21.899 --> 00:09:26.959
Compared to the freedom of the surface, the
dark and endless waters beneath it are associated

00:09:26.959 --> 00:09:29.399
with danger and the unknown.

00:09:29.399 --> 00:09:34.389
It is in this weightless realm, where ancient
worlds lie hidden, terrible monsters lurk

00:09:34.389 --> 00:09:37.639
and old secrets and treasures wait to be discovered.

00:09:37.639 --> 00:09:42.459
While the ocean may be by far the biggest
setting in the story world of One Piece, apart

00:09:42.459 --> 00:09:48.000
from a few exceptions, it is mostly the medium
to travel from one adventure to the next.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:53.149
The real setting, where most of the plot and
screen time takes place are the islands that

00:09:53.149 --> 00:09:55.110
lie on its surface.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:59.540
Not only do the islands serve as a representation
of the suppression by the world government,

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:04.269
they are also perfectly suited for an episodic
story like One Piece.

00:10:04.269 --> 00:10:08.720
Being completely isolated by the rest of the
world, an island is the perfect premise to

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.970
explore a distinct social context.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:17.279
Having a small and easily comprehensible culture
and philosophy on every new island is the

00:10:17.279 --> 00:10:22.230
perfect chance to create individual story
arcs with their own subplot.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:27.399
This makes every island into a unique setting
where new things can be tested, and individual

00:10:27.399 --> 00:10:30.370
development becomes very pronounced.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:36.449
One way this is often utilized in the context
of Anime and Manga is in the context of training,

00:10:36.449 --> 00:10:40.769
where one´s abilities can grow and develop
in an isolated place and where development

00:10:40.769 --> 00:10:42.910
can easily be compared.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:47.829
In the context of One Piece this often takes
place in the form of battle against a villain,

00:10:47.829 --> 00:10:49.850
that dominates said island.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:54.519
In that sense every island is also a miniature
of the world at large.

00:10:54.519 --> 00:10:59.370
All of this allows for a very complex and
detail-rich experience, which in turn works

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:03.230
perfectly with the visual capabilities of
Anime and Manga.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:08.930
Typically, an island is integrated into the
plot as follows: First, the characters from

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:13.769
the world we are familiar with arrive in a
new place with distinct rules and values.

00:11:13.769 --> 00:11:19.800
Then there is some sort of struggle or challenge
that has to be overcome, usually a villain.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:25.529
Finally, this conflict then has to be solved,
which involves personal growth by the protagonists.

00:11:25.529 --> 00:11:30.149
This premise allows the author to experiment
with new concepts and ideas.

00:11:30.149 --> 00:11:35.269
In One Piece in particular, but also in other
stories, these islands often also have different

00:11:35.269 --> 00:11:37.260
natural settings themselves.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:41.069
Some resemble deserts, others mountains and
again others jungles.

00:11:41.069 --> 00:11:46.759
Thus, a broad variety of settings can be utilized
and explored while at the same time still

00:11:46.759 --> 00:11:50.350
following the overall theme of the island.

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:53.870
Another important part of physical worldbuilding
is the weather.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:58.930
While at first glance this might not sound
very exciting, weather has a profound and

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:02.059
striking influence on the mood and emotion
of a scene.

00:12:02.059 --> 00:12:06.930
A good writer knows how to use the weather
to make the inner life of a character visible

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.730
to the audience.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:13.649
Depending on the context, most weather phenomena
can have positive or negative connotations

00:12:13.649 --> 00:12:14.649
alike.

00:12:14.649 --> 00:12:21.120
Let´s look at a few examples: Lightning and
thunder can represent passion or terror.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:27.720
Rain can be a sign of coziness or sadness.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:32.220
Wind can be relief and tension alike.

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:39.139
The sun can symbolize happiness, but also
a false exterior.

00:12:39.139 --> 00:12:45.579
And snow can make a scene feel very peaceful,
but it can also signify death.

00:12:45.579 --> 00:12:49.709
Next time you watch an intense scene, make
sure to pay attention to the weather and see

00:12:49.709 --> 00:12:54.209
how it used to enhance and intensify the characters
emotions.

00:12:54.209 --> 00:12:59.110
To round things off, let´s now look at some
other important elements of the story world,

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:03.319
that create a more fascinating and organic
experience for the reader.

00:13:03.319 --> 00:13:09.459
These are elements that aren´t 100% necessary
for a story to be great, but if used correctly

00:13:09.459 --> 00:13:11.440
can make a huge difference.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:17.380
One of these elements, that is being used
in One Piece is the concept of the vehicle.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:22.100
Luffy and his crew travel on board of a ship,
that brings them from A to B. However, this

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:26.569
ship also represents a sort of home for the
protagonists.

00:13:26.569 --> 00:13:32.079
It is a moving house that gives the audience
a sense of safety and comfort.

00:13:32.079 --> 00:13:36.910
Once the house is left, a new adventure begins
in the dangerous world outside.

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:42.870
This helps us form a sense of continuity by
serving as an anchor point, despite the ever-changing

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.380
landscape.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:50.449
Another great element to shift the perspective
of the viewer is to play around with size.

00:13:50.449 --> 00:13:54.970
One Piece is a story that particularly likes
to play with the concept of size in terms

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:58.490
of landscape, creatures or architecture.

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:03.240
Enormous constructions and beings have a profound
impact on the readers experience.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:08.329
No matter if it´s the gigantic gates of justice,
enormous sea monsters or the size of some

00:14:08.329 --> 00:14:10.279
of the characters involved.

00:14:10.279 --> 00:14:15.550
Having them put in contrast with our perception
of normal lets us witness the world, we thought

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:21.089
we knew, from a new perspective and allow
for an exciting shift in perception.

00:14:21.089 --> 00:14:25.300
Then of course there is technology and culture
as a whole.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:29.750
Having a unique set of machines and weapons
as well as distinct religious or cultural

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:34.629
concepts integrated into the world in a way
that feels natural, broadens our view of this

00:14:34.629 --> 00:14:36.079
world immensely.

00:14:36.079 --> 00:14:41.879
Especially in Anime and Manga, but also in
other fantasy series, this often includes

00:14:41.879 --> 00:14:46.670
magical powers or other forms of power systems,
that are woven into the world.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:52.690
I the context of One Piece, these are the
concepts of Haki or willpower and the so-called

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:57.199
Devil Fruits, that bestow unique powers upon
those that consume them.

00:14:57.199 --> 00:15:01.449
These systems have to follow distinct rules
that explain, why the world is the world it

00:15:01.449 --> 00:15:06.850
is and why the characters ended up with the
level of knowledge, power and technology that

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:08.170
they have.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:12.869
Last but not least, I want to mention the
use of gateways to other worlds, that can

00:15:12.869 --> 00:15:18.470
be used to create a harsh cut in between scenes
and locations and throw the hero into unknown

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:19.509
territory.

00:15:19.509 --> 00:15:24.470
In One Piece, this concept is used quite often,
like entering the dangerous grand line through

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:29.249
reverse mountain, visiting the fishman island
located at the bottom of the ocean by diving

00:15:29.249 --> 00:15:34.110
into the depth of the sea or entering the
underwater prison Impel Down, that resembles

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:35.670
Dante´s Inferno.

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:41.170
All of these elements are important pieces
that help establish a story world that feels

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:44.179
organic and structurally consistent.

00:15:44.179 --> 00:15:48.170
When you look at other stories that you enjoy
you will see these principals reoccurring,

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.699
as long as the author knows what he is doing.

00:15:50.699 --> 00:15:54.850
Of course, there are many more elements and
settings to be explored that have different

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.740
rules and implications.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:59.350
And of course, rules are also meant to be
broken.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:04.649
However, whatever variation is put on a concept
it must still make sense in the context of

00:16:04.649 --> 00:16:07.110
the story that is being told.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:12.459
Specifically, in Anime and Manga, worldbuilding
is one of the most important pieces.

00:16:12.459 --> 00:16:18.209
With its often romantic and solemn vibe, bringing
a unique story world to life is in a way the

00:16:18.209 --> 00:16:20.792
secret ingredient of this genre.

00:16:20.792 --> 00:16:27.379
This is what makes worldbuilding so important.

00:16:27.379 --> 00:16:31.379
